.TH SMITHPROXY-CFTAR 1 "November 2026" "smithproxy" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
smithproxy-cftar \- inspect and edit Smithproxy configuration archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smithproxy-cftar
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B smithproxy-cftar
.BR interactive | -i
.I archive.cftar
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smithproxy-cftar
operates on an offline Smithproxy CFtar archive. It does not modify the
configuration currently running inside a Smithproxy process.
.PP
Mutating commands validate the complete candidate archive, take the shared
publication lock, reject stale input, preserve the previous generation, and
atomically publish the replacement.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create --config FILE --startup FILE --output FILE
Create a new archive. Additional resources may be supplied with
.B --file ARCHIVE_PATH=FILE
or
.BR --executable " ARCHIVE_PATH=FILE" .
.TP
.B verify FILE
Validate the TAR structure, manifest, required entries, paths, and limits.
.TP
.B inspect FILE
Print the archive path, content hash, and entry count.
.TP
.B list FILE [PREFIX]
List entries, optionally restricted to a logical path prefix.
.TP
.B get FILE ARCHIVE_PATH
Write one validated archive entry to standard output.
.TP
.B resource import FILE ARCHIVE_PATH SOURCE [executable]
Import one resource and atomically publish the new archive generation.
.TP
.B resource export FILE ARCHIVE_PATH DESTINATION
Export one resource into a newly created filesystem file.
.TP
.B resource remove FILE ARCHIVE_PATH
Remove one resource and atomically publish the new archive generation.
.TP
.B interactive FILE
Open the small offline administration shell. The
.B -i
alias is equivalent.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Interactive mode provides inspect, list, show, validate, diff, edit, import,
export, remove, save, discard, expose, close, and quit operations. Changes
remain in an isolated working copy until
.B save
is explicitly requested.
.PP
Exposed resources are read-only temporary files owned by the interactive
session and are removed when closed or when the session exits.
.SH CONCURRENCY
The tool shares the CFtar publication lock with Smithproxy. Publication fails
if the archive changed after the session was opened; reopen the archive and
repeat the intended change against the new generation.
.PP
When Smithproxy observes a valid external replacement, it marks the startup
configuration as requiring restart. The running configuration is not changed
automatically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/smithproxy/smithproxy.cftar
Default native Smithproxy configuration archive.
.TP
.I ARCHIVE.cftar.lock
Sidecar publication lock shared by the daemon and offline tools.
.TP
.I ARCHIVE.cftar.previous
Recovery generation retained during successful publication.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. One indicates an operational or validation failure.
Two indicates invalid command-line usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smithproxy (1),
.BR smithproxy.cfg (5)
